                                    <watches>3</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="18031049" author="JIRAUSER298472" created="Mon, 20 Oct 2025 03:24:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Root Cause&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Due to a Calcite version upgrade, a feature was introduced that removes ORDER BY clauses inside subqueries.&lt;br/&gt;
This feature is enabled by default, causing the subquery ORDER BY to be ignored during RelNode parsing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Dev Design&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
A new system-level configuration is introduced:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;sub&gt;kylin.query.calcite.remove-sort-in-subquery&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
The default value is false, which means Kylin will keep the ORDER BY clause in subqueries instead of removing it.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
